### Setup Compute Nodes

With the compute nodes running their freshly installed base OS, configure them
for OpenHPC use. Commands are run on all nodes in parallel with `xdsh`, xCAT's
native distributed shell.

The remaining steps install packages directly on the running compute nodes
with the package manager, which requires the nodes to reach the distribution,
EPEL, and OpenHPC package repositories. By default xCAT points the compute
default route at the head node; ensure this provides a path to the
repositories (for example via NAT on the head node or a site gateway
registered in the xCAT `networks` table), or host a local repository mirror
on the head node and register it on the computes instead.

We first disable the firewall on the compute nodes.
<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_if [ "${xcat_mode}" = "stateful" ] -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Configure HTTPS proxy for compute nodes (site-specific) -->
<!-- ohpc_command #<<< ohpc_proxy:compute >>># -->
<!-- ohpc_end -->

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Disable firewall on compute nodes -->
```bash
# Disable firewall for computes
xdsh compute systemctl disable --now firewalld
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

The *compute* nodes need access to the EPEL repository, a required dependency
for OpenHPC packages.
<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Configure access to EPEL repo on compute nodes -->
```bash
# Add EPEL repo
{{ pkg_install_chroot }} epel-release
# Enable CRB
{{ compute_run("/usr/bin/crb enable") }}
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

And add additional packages.
<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Add additional packages to compute nodes -->
```bash
# Add Network Time Protocol (NTP) support and point it at the head node
{{ pkg_install_chroot }} chrony
{{ compute_run("echo server ${sms_ip} iburst >> /etc/chrony.conf") }}
{{ compute_run("systemctl enable --now chronyd") }}

# Include nfs-utils
{{ pkg_install_chroot }} nfs-utils
```
<!-- ohpc_fi -->
<!-- ohpc_end -->
